free.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Koyeb / Render (Direct GitHub Deployment)\nBoth platforms let you connect your GitHub repo and deploy with zero card required on signup:\n* **Koyeb:** Offers a free Eco container tier. Deploy directly from your `stream-vault` GitHub repository in 2 clicks.\n* **Render:** Free web service tier (750 hours/month free). Automatically redeploys whenever you `git push` to your repository.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Run Locally on Your PC + Free Cloudflare Tunnel\nSince you already have Python 3.14 installed on your Windows machine:\n* The bot runs on your computer with **zero restrictions**, using your own hard drive space for temporary downloads.\n* For the **Direct Stream Links (DDL)**, you can use **Cloudflare Tunnels** (`cloudflared`):\n  * 100% free, zero signup walls or credit cards.\n  * Gives your local bot an official, secure public HTTPS URL (e.g., `https://your-bot.trycloudflare.com/stream/...`) so you can stream movies on your phone or VLC even when away from home.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Step\nLet's build and test everything on your **Local PC first**. \n\nOnce we verify that the scraper, the Telegram bot, and the streaming links work smoothly, we can add a 1-click `Dockerfile` so you can deploy it to **Hugging Face Spaces** or **Koyeb** whenever you want 24/7 cloud uptime—completely free, without ever needing a credit card.\n\nShall we begin **Step 1** (setting up the dependency checker and core files)?","thinking":"The user's issue centers on the Oracle Cloud Free Tier's credit card requirement. The central problem is the user's lack of a credit card, preventing access to the free tier. This necessitates identifying alternative, truly free cloud options that do not require credit card verification.\n\n\nSeveral credit card-free options are available: running the application locally using tools like Cloudflare Tunnels for public access; employing cloud container platforms such as Koyeb, Render, or Hugging Face Spaces; utilizing GitHub Codespaces' free monthly quota; or leveraging Google Cloud Shell or Colab for on-demand runs. Koyeb, Render, and Hugging Face Spaces seem particularly suitable due to their free tiers and deployment simplicity.\n\n\n"}
